2026/05/05 08:07:35 INFO dspy.teleprompt.simba_utils: Advice for nl2pln.predict: If the input describes ordinal stages/rounds such as “first round”, “second round”, “third round” and what each used/contained, do not encode the whole fact as one opaque predicate like `(: s1 (RoundUsedWordCategory spellingContest firstRound animalWords) (STV 1.0 1.0))`. Instead create separate stable entities and modifier facts: a contest entity, one `Round` entity per ordinal, one `Words` entity per word set, ordinal predicates such as `(First round1)`, `(Second round2)`, `(Third round3)`, category predicates such as `(Animal words1)`, `(Plant words2)`, `(Weather words3)`, and a simple relation `(Used round1 words1)`, `(Used round2 words2)`, `(Used round3 words3)`. For a spelling-contest example, use facts like `(: s3 (Round round1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s4 (First round1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s7 (Animal words1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s8 (Used round1 words1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, and similarly for `round2/words2/Plant` and `round3/words3/Weather`. When later asked “Which round used plant/weather words?”, reuse the word entity already marked by `(Plant words2)` or `(Weather words3)` and query the smallest relation that binds the round, e.g. `(: $prf (Used $round words2) $tv)` or, if the word entity is not fixed, a two-conjunct query like `(: $prf (And (Used $round $words) (Plant $words)) $tv)`. When asked “What kind of words did the first round use?”, resolve `first` to the entity with `(First round1)` and query the used word set with the category constraint, e.g. `(: $prf (And (Used round1 $words) (Animal $words)) $tv)`. Avoid inventing new predicates during question translation; reuse `Round`, `First/Second/Third`, `Words`, category predicates, and `Used` from context. Also avoid unnecessary three-or-more-conjunct `And` queries such as adding `(Round $round)` when `(Used $round words3)` is already enough, because broader conjunctions are more likely to time out.
