2026/05/05 08:09:05 INFO dspy.teleprompt.simba_utils: Advice for nl2pln.predict: If the input contains speech/reporting verbs such as told, said, asked, informed, warned, or asked whether, then model each speech act as a reified event with separate role facts, not as one custom n-ary predicate with a nested proposition. For a sentence like Mira told the hikers that the north trail was closed after the storm, prefer facts of the form `(: s9 (Told tell1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s10 (Agent tell1 mira) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s11 (Recipient tell1 hikers1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s12 (Content tell1 close1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, plus reified content facts like `(: s6 (Closed close1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s7 (Patient close1 trail1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, `(: s8 (After close1 storm1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, and entity/modifier facts such as `(Hikers hikers1)`, `(Trail trail1)`, `(North trail1)`, `(Storm storm1)`. Avoid encodings like `(: s1 (Tell Mira hikers (TrailClosed northTrail afterStorm)) ...)` or `(: s2 (Ask Mira (HasPrintedMap anyone)) ...)`, because later variable queries over those nested multi-argument predicates are much more likely to time out. Resolve pronouns before adding facts, so She in the second sentence becomes `mira`, and reuse lowercase stable constants. For an asking event whose content may be asked about later, add an explicit content link for the ask event, e.g. `(: s18 (Content ask1 askContent1) (STV 1.0 1.0))`, with simple supporting facts tying `askContent1` to the printed-map question; do not treat `anyone` as a concrete person who has the map. When converting follow-up questions using an existing context, first identify the relevant event constant from the context and query the smallest direct role fact: for What did Mira tell the hikers?, use `(: $prf (Content tell1 $what) $tv)`; for Who did Mira tell about the closed trail?, use `(: $prf (Recipient tell1 $who) $tv)`; for What did Mira ask?, use `(: $prf (Content ask1 $what) $tv)` only if a matching Content fact was added. If multiple events are possible, use a small constrained `And` to identify the event, but once the event constant is known, prefer a direct role query. Always keep the bare query scaffold exactly `(: $prf <type-pattern> $tv)` with variable proof and TV slots, and reuse the exact predicates/constants already present in context.
