2026/05/05 11:23:40 INFO dspy.teleprompt.simba_utils: Advice for nl2pln.predict: When translating locative existence sentences like "There is a silver key under the doormat at the blue cottage", create separate entity/modifier facts and generic spatial relations: e.g. `(Key key1)`, `(Silver key1)`, `(Doormat doormat1)`, `(Cottage cottage1)`, `(Blue cottage1)`, `(Under key1 doormat1)`, `(At doormat1 cottage1)`, and preferably also `(At key1 cottage1)`. Do not bake modifiers into constants such as `blue_cottage`, and do not omit landmark types like `Doormat` or `Cottage`. For negative existence sentences like "No spare key is hanging by the back door", still create the entity/modifier facts, e.g. `(Key spare_key1)`, `(Spare spare_key1)`, `(Door back_door1)`, `(Back back_door1)`, then encode the denied relation as a zero-strength fact such as `(: s13 (Hanging spare_key1 back_door1) (STV 0.0 1.0))`; avoid one-off predicates like `HangingByBackDoor`. When later answering questions from this context, add no new statements and reuse the exact existing constants. Avoid multi-clause `And` queries for these simple location/existence questions because they can time out. For "What is under the doormat at the blue cottage?", after resolving `doormat1` as the doormat at the blue cottage, prefer the narrow query `(: $prf (Under $x doormat1) $tv)`; if verification is needed, issue separate small ground queries like `(: $prf (At doormat1 cottage1) $tv)` and `(: $prf (Blue cottage1) $tv)` rather than one `And`. For "Is there a spare key hanging by the back door?", resolve `spare_key1` and `back_door1` from context and query the decisive ground fact `(: $prf (Hanging spare_key1 back_door1) $tv)` so the returned STV 0.0 supports the answer "No". For "Where is the silver key?", resolve `key1` from `(Key key1)` and `(Silver key1)` and query simple location facts such as `(: $prf (Under key1 $where) $tv)` plus, if the full phrase is needed, separate follow-up queries `(: $prf (At $where $place) $tv)` or `(: $prf (At key1 $place) $tv)` and `(: $prf (Blue $place) $tv)`.
